lesson: 236
title: Dice
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: An ordinary die has 6 faces with 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6 dots.
explain: All the dots on one die: 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6 = 21.
explain: So 4 dice have 4 × 21 = 84 dots in all.
vars: a=name n=2..6 k=2..9
answer: n * 21
exercise: How many dots are there on {n} dice altogether?
exercise: {a} has {n} dice. How many dots are on all their faces?
exercise: A game comes with {n} dice. How many spots are there on the dice in total?
exercise: {a} paints the dots on {n} wooden dice. How many dots does {a.he} paint?
exercise: Count all the dots on {n} ordinary dice. How many are there?
exercise: got {n} dice here, how many dots on em all
exercise: {n+1} dice, no wait one's lost, {n}. how many dots all together
exercise: bro says {n*6} dots on {n} dice lol. nah count every face, how many dots
exercise: making dice in art class, {n} of them, how many dots do i draw, oh and they're blue
exercise: {n} dice in the box from the games cupboard. dots total?
test: What is the total number of pips on {n} dice?
test: If every face of {n} dice is counted, how many spots are there?
test: {a} turns each of {n} dice over and over to count all its dots. How many dots does {a.he} count?
test: how many spots on {n} dice, every side
test: {n} dice, {k} board games in the cupboard too, how many dots on the dice
test: A set of {n} standard dice: how many dots in all?
exam: Determine the aggregate number of pips inscribed upon all faces of {n.words} standard dice.
exam: Ascertain the total number of dots borne by the faces of a set of {n} standard dice.
exam: Compute the sum of all spots appearing on {n} ordinary dice, each face being taken into account.
exam: Whereas {a} possesses {n} standard dice, state the number of dots thereupon.
exercise: Grandad passed away and left {a} his old box of {n} dice. How many dots are there on them altogether?
exercise: dad got the sack so no new games this year, sod it, we've still got {n} dice. how many dots on the lot?
test: {a}'s little brother was economical with the truth: he said he had lost the dice, but all {n} were under his bed. How many dots are on the dice he hid?
